" role="presentation"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline></svg></span></div><div data-rid="e8260ed5-34c2-49dd-8305-8adeb8253451" class="r-jnaswl alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Excess Prostaglandins</p></span></div></div></button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="radix-:Raj2:-content-5821c885-5eeb-450e-9cb0-91b3986a07611" data-state="inactive" id="radix-:Raj2:-trigger-5821c885-5eeb-450e-9cb0-91b3986a07611" style="display:contents" data-replo-tabs-trigger="true" tabindex="-1" data-orientation="vertical" data-radix-collection-item=""><div data-rid="5821c885-5eeb-450e-9cb0-91b3986a0761" tabindex="0" class="r-kn1wf3"><div data-rid="f7df7823-c6d4-44dc-9ca2-db9a1a4268a2" class="r-181fi2x"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-check-circle" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="presentation"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline></svg></span></div><div data-rid="b37040f6-4088-405c-9204-24fb728bdb2b" class="r-152qjjj alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Hormonal imbalance</p></span></div></div></button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="radix-:Raj2:-content-1feb33d2-c71a-4bd6-be04-1c909bc2897a2" data-state="inactive" id="radix-:Raj2:-trigger-1feb33d2-c71a-4bd6-be04-1c909bc2897a2" style="display:contents" data-replo-tabs-trigger="true" tabindex="-1" data-orientation="vertical" data-radix-collection-item=""><div data-rid="1feb33d2-c71a-4bd6-be04-1c909bc2897a" tabindex="0" class="r-tmx8oi"><div data-rid="6f494315-d6e6-4fd1-b80b-a2a0784b821b" class="r-yibpbt"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-check-circle" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="presentation"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline></svg></span></div><div data-rid="1f298f50-88b0-465e-b826-70609c9d3ea0" class="r-bfhr4b alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Micronutrient gaps</p></span></div></div></button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="radix-:Raj2:-content-1238416a-f0cc-49c4-8f57-ce1f07f78f1c3" data-state="inactive" id="radix-:Raj2:-trigger-1238416a-f0cc-49c4-8f57-ce1f07f78f1c3" style="display:contents" data-replo-tabs-trigger="true" tabindex="-1" data-orientation="vertical" data-radix-collection-item=""><div data-rid="1238416a-f0cc-49c4-8f57-ce1f07f78f1c" tabindex="0" class="r-kmtb1h"><div data-rid="e84e63fd-bac2-4168-b3e7-f0735af24052" class="r-fpuoc6"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-check-circle" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="presentation"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline></svg></span></div><div data-rid="0739a66b-01d1-48ab-9817-db0906eeb28c" class="r-vqltyt alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Cloudlike Comfort</p></span></div></div></button></div></div></div><div data-rid="a3951eae-bbc7-4613-bbfd-8d7ea38114f3" class="r-nbzbib"><div data-state="active" data-orientation="vertical" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="radix-:Raj2:-trigger-7cbb6c4e-4f13-40a0-8cd6-4975cd72ced30" id="radix-:Raj2:-content-7cbb6c4e-4f13-40a0-8cd6-4975cd72ced30" tabindex="0" style="display:contents;animation-duration:0s"><div data-rid="587a92f4-9981-4824-80a9-0debbc206645" class="r-1iutt3y"><picture data-rid="0eb1d7ea-3c20-4ef0-b599-c0bcf820d7c1" class="r-1fmy9l7"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/f09a2e0e-927a-4f69-82ae-43ad94c1060f?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/72bde649-df8d-40dc-8bba-8c162a442d79?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/72bde649-df8d-40dc-8bba-8c162a442d79?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/72bde649-df8d-40dc-8bba-8c162a442d79" alt="Triangle diagram labeled &#x27;The Pain Triangle&#x27; with hormonal imbalance, micronutrient gaps, excess prostaglandins." class="r-qtofc9" loading="eager"/></picture><div data-rid="99e0822b-5f50-49d1-8c9c-075dbb45945a" class="r-4tzu96 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Excess Prostaglandins</p></span></div><div data-rid="316678e5-f230-4e94-ba0d-3ccfe2bdbfa7" class="r-j2kdb5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Prostaglandins are essential and help your uterus shed its lining. However, when they surge — due to an an overactive COX-2 enzyme — they directly intensify cramps, sharpen pain signals, and make them more frequent.</p><br><p>Painkillers work by blocking prostaglandins after they’ve spiked, often hitting COX-1 (needed for stomach protection) along with COX-2. This can lead to side effects like indigestion or ulcers —while leaving hormonal and nutrient imbalances unresolved, so the cycle of pain keeps repeating.</p></span></div></div></div><div data-state="inactive" data-orientation="vertical" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="radix-:Raj2:-trigger-5821c885-5eeb-450e-9cb0-91b3986a07611" id="radix-:Raj2:-content-5821c885-5eeb-450e-9cb0-91b3986a07611" tabindex="0" style="display:none"><div data-rid="91c5cd89-8d60-4172-b8fa-b4fed4dd53f6" class="r-10s53mp"><picture data-rid="1d1842eb-5526-4cdc-b9ea-ae34fb14142d" class="r-b0h80f"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/f09a2e0e-927a-4f69-82ae-43ad94c1060f?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/72bde649-df8d-40dc-8bba-8c162a442d79?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/72bde649-df8d-40dc-8bba-8c162a442d79?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/72bde649-df8d-40dc-8bba-8c162a442d79" alt="Triangle diagram labeled &#x27;The Pain Triangle&#x27; with hormonal imbalance, micronutrient gaps, excess prostaglandins." class="r-1ohmv47" loading="eager"/></picture><div data-rid="f47ad30e-dbc3-480e-b16e-e6c0b0bbb0be" class="r-1k38fb4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Hormonal Imbalance</p></span></div><div data-rid="fba7e7db-b511-448d-9537-1a1c6a8892e6" class="r-1yckb9n alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(112, 121, 136)">Your hormones naturally rise and fall each month. But when oestrogen rises too high (often under everyday stress, hectic schedules, bad sleep, or poor diet), it triggers an overproduction of prostaglandins — the main driver behind deeper cramps and inflammation.</span><br><br><span style="color: rgb(112, 121, 136)">The result? With this natural balance lost, you´re left facing heightened cramping, and fewer defenses against pain flares. If you don’t have a condition like PCOS or endometriosis, studies indicate that the difference between someone with debilitating cramps and someone who barely notices theirs comes down to prostaglandin levels.</span></p></span></div></div></div><div data-state="inactive" data-orientation="vertical" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="radix-:Raj2:-trigger-1feb33d2-c71a-4bd6-be04-1c909bc2897a2" id="radix-:Raj2:-content-1feb33d2-c71a-4bd6-be04-1c909bc2897a2" tabindex="0" style="display:none"><div data-rid="82df12df-9a4a-425b-b2b6-1219ca01e359" class="r-10262nv"><picture data-rid="786f8b13-952d-4edd-90de-0b954ed2150e" class="r-1dlwi1g"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/f09a2e0e-927a-4f69-82ae-43ad94c1060f?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/72bde649-df8d-40dc-8bba-8c162a442d79?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/72bde649-df8d-40dc-8bba-8c162a442d79?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/72bde649-df8d-40dc-8bba-8c162a442d79" class="r-c6pnab" loading="eager"/></picture><div data-rid="02fd31af-e3e5-4b3a-b7ab-dc5e9a255d57" class="r-1dxuzw3 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Micronutrient gaps</p></span></div><div data-rid="88ab6c0a-fa6b-426b-ae42-e3edba71faaf" class="r-13okead alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>A woman's body relies on micronutrients to manage cramps, energize muscles, and regulate inflammation. But monthly blood loss, combined with fast-paced living or less-than-ideal nutrition, can leave reserves depleted. A 2024 study led by Harvard researchers found that many UK women have at least five major micronutrient gaps.*</p></span></div></div></div><div data-state="inactive" data-orientation="vertical" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="radix-:Raj2:-trigger-1238416a-f0cc-49c4-8f57-ce1f07f78f1c3" id="radix-:Raj2:-content-1238416a-f0cc-49c4-8f57-ce1f07f78f1c3" tabindex="